GREEN implementation step for epic sturm-8aq3. Lands the actual swap rewrite that turns sturm-8dzd and sturm-hfzc green.

Edit point (only): `include/sturm/qtypes/lossy_oop.hpp:58-65`.

Rewrite:

```cpp
template <std::size_t W>
inline void swap(qint_t<W>& a, qint_t<W>& b) noexcept {
    sturm_backend_context_t* raw = sturm_get_thread_context();
    if (!raw || raw->control_stack.depth() == 0u) {
        // depth 0 (or no context): classical relabel — zero gates.
        using std::swap;
        swap(a.value, b.value);
        swap(a.super_mask, b.super_mask);
        swap(a.qubits, b.qubits);
        swap(a.owning_, b.owning_);
        return;
    }
    // depth >= 1: per-bit Fredkin via DSL. BitProxy::operator^= ->
    // ensure_quantum() updates super_mask per bit, so the 3-CNOT
    // chain inside lib_swap_dsl propagates per-bit superposition
    // state correctly. value/owning_ are intentionally NOT swapped:
    // under control they cannot hold a single classical truth.
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < W; ++i) {
        BitProxy ai(a, i), bi(b, i);
        lib_swap_dsl(ai, bi);
    }
}
```

New include needed in `lossy_oop.hpp`: `#include "sturm/lib/swap_dsl.hpp"` (header-only, lightweight).

Why no STURM_REGISTER_ADJOINT for swap: Fredkin is self-inverse, and the LO-2 scope-exit cleanup re-emits the same `swap(a, tmp)` token before `*_oop_adj` (`transpiler/src/lossy_scope_exit_emitter.{hpp,cpp}`). With the new behavior, the reverse swap auto-lifts identically and self-cancels at gate level.

Why `owning_` is not swapped on the controlled branch: under `WHEN(ctrl)` the qubits genuinely belong to their original owner on the `ctrl=0` branch; the gate-level Fredkin handles the conditional state. Forward+reverse swap pair is symmetric, so destructor-time release lands on the right indices.

